BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibition: Stars & Stripes - The American Flag from 9/11 to 250
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTSTAMP:20261118T191440Z
UID:2dee3dd24987876baebf5ed4155e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:2026 marks the momentous occasion of the United States celebra
 ting 250 years as a nation\, and also marks 25 years since the 9/11 terror
 ist attacks. This September\, Slater Memorial Museum of Norwich Free Acade
 my brings to life a display of memories as captured by artist and author R
 obert Carley. Carley’s documentation of post-9/11 America showcases vivi
 d and meaningful images of the American flag across the country\, expresse
 d in dozens of different forms.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/exhi
 bition-stars-stripes-american-flag-911-250
LOCATION:Converse Gallery\, Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\,
  Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/exhibition-stars-stripes-american-flag-911-
 250
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hieroglyphs to Hype: The Modern Afterlife of Ancient Egypt
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTSTAMP:20261118T191440Z
UID:11204f08b00e7472a22ffdd9779c@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Hieroglyphs to Hype: The Modern Afterlife of Ancient Egypt wil
 l explore the enduring fascination with ancient Egyptian art and culture (
 dubbed “Egyptomania” by 19th-century Europeans) through a selection of
  paintings\, prints\, photographs\, and decorative art ranging from the ea
 rly 19th century through the present day. These objects\, from the humble 
 to the refined\, from the shamelessly commercial to the Afrofuturist\, rep
 resent the range of artistic responses to – and misconceptions about –
  ancient Egyptian visual culture.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/hi
 eroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-egypt
LOCATION:Bellarmine Hall\, Bellarmine Hall Galleries\, 1073 N. Benson Road
 \, Fairfield CT\, 06824-3826
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/hieroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-e
 gypt
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hieroglyphs to Hype: The Modern Afterlife of Ancient Egypt
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTSTAMP:20261118T191440Z
UID:4cee5dc74f5005488862f3d393cf@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This exhibition will explore the enduring fascination with anc
 ient Egyptian art and culture (dubbed “Egyptomania” by 19th-century Eu
 ropeans) through a selection of paintings\, prints\, photographs\, and dec
 orative art ranging from the early 19th century through the present day. T
 hese objects\, from the humble to the refined\, from the shamelessly comme
 rcial to the Afrofuturist\, represent the range of artistic responses to 
 – and misconceptions about – ancient Egyptian visual culture.\n\nSourc
 e: https://ctvisit.com/events/hieroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-eg
 ypt-0
LOCATION:Bellarmine Hall Galleries\, 1073 North Benson Road\, Fairfield CT
 \, 06824
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/hieroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-e
 gypt-0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:James Welling: Cento
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTSTAMP:20261118T191440Z
UID:7339357a303a56796091545c0b6c@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:This exhibition focuses on more than 60 recent works by photog
 rapher James Welling (American\, born 1951). From the artist’s Cento and
  Personae series\, these photographs of ancient sites in Italy and Greece
 \, as well as antiquities found in museums around the world\, were subject
 ed to digital and painterly alteration by the artist to achieve transforma
 tive effects. The photographs will be exhibited alongside a selection from
  the Museum’s extensive historic plaster cast collection of Greek and Ro
 man sculpture.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/james-welling-cento
LOCATION:Quick Center for the Arts\, Walsh Gallery\, 1073 N. Benson Road\,
  Bellarmine Hall - Art Museum\, Fairfield CT\, 06824-3826
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/james-welling-cento
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Live Here
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTSTAMP:20261118T191440Z
UID:561fc4d7ef1ba7afe9fe435470b7@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:An exhibition that looks at housing as the framework of commun
 ity life. With historical images\, photography\, architectural designs\, r
 esident testimony\, and interactive displays\, We Live Here will place a c
 entury of residential life in the greater New London area and Connecticut 
 in the broader context of the nation. The history of dwelling is our socia
 l history. It illuminates how our communities live now and could live bett
 er in the future.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
LOCATION:The Garde Gallery\, Garde Arts Center\, 305 State Street\, New Lo
 ndon CT\, 06320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/we-live-here
END:VEVENT
